% A multi-literal query projects the named variables in order of first
% appearance and drops the anonymous ones, so the columns here are
% X, Y, L and the edge(_, X) literal contributes nothing but a filter.  A
% blank line separates one query's rows from the next, and -q queries run
% after the embedded ones.
edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).
edge(c, d).

label(b, beta).
label(c, gamma).

edge(X, Y), label(Y, L), edge(_, X)?
